# Shared files touched by wave 2 (PDF), diffed against the branch base a90208e9d.
# One line per file saying why; the diffs follow in the same order.
#   .gitattributes            the vendored OCR engine, HarfBuzz and the Noto fonts kept byte for byte (-text / binary) so the READMEs' sha256 sums match
#   assets/app.css            WAVE-2 block only (appended between the markers): page grids, file-row drag, progress/Cancel, password rows, live preview, draggable items, crop editor, Scan to PDF cards and camera, text output wrapping
#   build-hubs.js             the /pdf/ hub intro names the new tools (compress, password, crop, picture, OCR, Word, text)
#   build/compare-extra.js    item G: /compare/free-pdf-editor gap list, table, groups and FAQ made true for the new tools (gap first, no product claims)
#   build/jobs.js             finder rows and card lines for the 11 new PDF tools
#   build/tests/claims/kit.js runPdf passes a password; specs with workerScripts load as their worker does; pdfcore gets the font loader in Node; upload waits for rows to finish loading; K.open(url, { intercept: false }) for pages whose workers interception would stall (OCR)
#   privacy/index.html        two lines: PDF tool settings and the invoice kept in local storage; Scan to PDF's camera only on request

diff --git a/.gitattributes b/.gitattributes
index 8be0b52df..365e605a1 100644
--- a/.gitattributes
+++ b/.gitattributes
@@ -25,3 +25,8 @@ engine/vendor/ort/** -text
 # models (and their 20 MiB .partN pieces) are binary: no line-ending
 # conversion, no text diff, and release.js's 0x08 scan skips them
 engine/models/** binary
+# The PDF tools' OCR engine, shaper and fonts, stored as published, so the
+# sha256 sums in their READMEs keep matching.
+engine/vendor/tesseract/** -text
+engine/vendor/harfbuzz/** -text
+engine/vendor/fonts/** binary
