     <li><strong>Showcase submissions (optional).</strong> If you send something you made to the <a href="/showcase/">showcase</a>, nothing leaves the page until you press the button. Then our server receives, and stores in Google Cloud Firestore in the Mumbai region (asia-south1), your name, any handle, the platform, the link, the tool you used, your one-line description, what you do (if you pick it), your email (if you leave one) and a note that you ticked the consent box, along with a one-way hash of your connection’s address that we use only to limit sending to five an hour. Nothing is published unless you ticked the consent box and we have approved it by hand. We then show your name, handle, platform, link, tool and description on the showcase and on the page of the tool you used, and use what you do, if you picked it, to list the entry with others in the same line of work. Your email is never shown; it is used only to tell you the entry is live. To have an entry taken down, ask on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> with the link to it: it comes off the site at the next update, and the stored submission is deleted by our daily clean-up once it is 90 days past the day it arrived (within a day, if it is already older). Approved entries stay, with their email and address hash, until you ask for them to be removed; pending and rejected submissions are deleted automatically 90 days after they arrive. The address hash is never published, and the hourly count kept against it is deleted after a day.</li>
     <li><strong>A theme preference.</strong> If you switch between light, dark or system theme, that single choice is saved in your browser's local storage so it's remembered next visit. It never leaves your device.</li>
     <li><strong>The last few tools you opened.</strong> So the homepage can offer them back to you, the names of your six most recent tools are saved in your browser's local storage. Only the names — never anything you entered into them. It never leaves your device, we cannot see it, and clearing your browser data removes it.</li>
+    <li><strong>PDF tool settings, and the invoice you are writing.</strong> The PDF tools remember the choices you make (a resolution, a position, a watermark's wording) in your browser's local storage, one entry per tool, so they are set the same next time; never page ranges, signatures or passwords. The Invoice Generator also keeps the invoice you are working on, your logo, the clients you save and your last invoice number there, until you press its "forget" button or clear your browser data. None of it leaves your device.</li>
+    <li><strong>The camera, only when you ask.</strong> Scan to PDF turns the camera on when you press its camera button and off when you press Done. The pictures are straightened and made into a PDF in the page; nothing is recorded or sent.</li>
     <li><strong>Hosting logs.</strong> This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub, Inc. may log IP addresses and request metadata for security and operational purposes, independently of us. See <a referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement?utm_source=1234tools.com&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=privacy&amp;utm_content=content" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
     <li><strong>Analytics, only with your consent.</strong> If you accept when asked, Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity record which pages you visit, roughly where in the world you are, and how you moved through the page. Clarity also replays page usage, with every form field, result panel and generated document masked, so what you enter into a tool is not captured. Advertising and personalisation signals are disabled and IP addresses are anonymised. See <a referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?utm_source=1234tools.com&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=privacy&amp;utm_content=content" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and <a referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement?utm_source=1234tools.com&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=privacy&amp;utm_content=content" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft's Privacy Statement</a>. Nothing loads until you agree, and a Global Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal is treated as a refusal.</li>
   </ul>
